{
  "case_id": "2010-09-751",
  "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court Clerk",
      "case_id": "2010-09-751",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nSEAN E. SUMMERS, ESQ., York, Pennsylvania; on behalf of\nPetitioner.\nMARGIE J. PHELPS, ESQ., Topeka, Kansas; on behalf of\nRespondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Sean E. Summers (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2010-09-751",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SUMMERS: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it\nplease the Court:\nWe are talking about a funeral. If context\nis ever going to matter, it has to matter in the context\nof a funeral. Mr. Snyder simply wanted to bury his son\nin a private, dignified manner. When the Respondents'\nbehavior made that impossible, Mr. Snyder was entitled\nto turn to the tort law of the State of Maryland."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-751",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Are we just talking about a funeral? That's one of the problems I have with the\ncase. There was also this video that -- that your\nclient watched, right, later, after the funeral?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-751",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Well, why does he have a\n-- a claim? As I understand it, after this case arose\nMaryland passed a statute putting time, place, and\nmanner restrictions. I read that statute, and it seems\nto me that there was nothing unlawful, nothing out of\ncompliance with that statute, that was done here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court Record",
      "case_id": "2010-09-751",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "they were positioned about 30 feet from the main vehicle entrance to the\nchurch, and they rerouted the funeral procession so they\nwere 200 to 300 feet away from there."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Sean E. Summers (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2010-09-751",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "they had a sign that said \"Priests Rape Boys\"; they had a sign that said \"God Hates You\"; \"You're Going to Hell.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Summers",
      "case_id": "2010-09-751",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the rule should be Hustler v. Falwell generally does not apply to a private figure unless the defendants can show some compelling connection there, and if you --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Phelps",
      "case_id": "2010-09-751",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When members of the Westboro Baptist Church entered an ongoing, extensive, public discussion and wide array of expressive activities taking place in direct connection with the deaths and funerals of soldiers killed in Iraq and Afghanistan, they did so with great circumspection, and they did so with an awareness of the boundaries that have been set by the precedents of this Court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2010-09-751",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Ms. Phelps, suppose -- suppose your group or another group or -- picks a wounded soldier and follows him around, demonstrates at his home, demonstrates at his workplace, demonstrates at his church, basically saying a lot of the things that were on these signs or -- or other offensive and outrageous things, and just follows this person around, day-to-day. Does that person not have a claim for intentional infliction of emotional distress?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-751",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The jury was not instructed to limit themselves to fighting words. No element of the torts under which liability attached included fighting words."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Phelps",
      "case_id": "2010-09-751",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If you stay within those bounds -- and under these torts even, this notion of exploiting, it has no definition in a principle of law that would guide people as to when they could or could not."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-751",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is it your -- is it your argument that the First Amendment never allows a claim for the intentional infliction of emotional distress based on speech unless the speech is such that it can be proven to be false or true?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-751",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But your argument depends on the proposition that this is speech on a matter of public concern; is that correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Phelps",
      "case_id": "2010-09-751",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the issue of race is a matter of public concern. I think approaching an individual up close and in their grill to berate them gets you out of the zone of protection, and we would never do that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Phelps",
      "case_id": "2010-09-751",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For harassing conduct, not for speech. Not for public speech, Justice Kennedy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-751",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Let's talk about subjectively. You're concerned about -- surely fighting words is -- you know, whether something is a fighting word, that's a very subjective call, isn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Phelps",
      "case_id": "2010-09-751",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I am not a fan of the fighting words doctrine. I do think it has problems. I just don't think it applies in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2010-09-751",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, suppose it's not disrupted and suppose -- and I know that this is -- that you contest these facts -- that yours wasn't disrupted, that they stopped when you started, that they were a sufficient number of feet away from the funeral and so forth."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-751",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The conduct has to be outrageous, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2010-09-751",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, that's true, but I was assuming a situation in which the -- a jury found that the \"war is wrong\" -- that a jury did find that outrageous, and the question was: Were we going to reverse the jury verdict because we -- the First Amendment prohibited it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2010-09-751",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
      "evidence_id": "unavailable-56abc0c68ed7-58",
